			<div class="content" id="post-content-2344107">
									

<p>Was an upvote, but fridge logic popped in: why is the maladjustment just vertical? Why is it &quot;invariably&quot; when they could theoretically correct the trajectory?<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-505580-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-505580-1')">1</a></sup> I mean, the science for this is real world based: the planet's orbit around hte sun isn't perfect, so even if you didn't use absolute universal coordinates, the same solar coordinates will leave you in a bad place.</p>
<p>Don't get me wrong, the concept of Nazi solders materializing in the present and immediately falling to their deaths is hilarious, but the construction leads me to nitpick. +0.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
