			<div class="content" id="post-content-2353041">
									

<p>Ok, it's about time I addressed this.</p>
<p>I'm going to write a supplement and/or tale that follows up and elaborates on this thing a bit sometime very soon, but what it boils down to is this: it's a calibration error put into place by a saboteur. The saboteur <em>could have</em> made this thing launch everyone who uses it into the sun or the cold vacuum of space or something, but instead, they turned a single adjusting dial just a few degrees off-center, so their work would be less visible.</p>
<p>The Foundation hasn't fixed it because the Ahnenerbe burned all of the blueprints, and the Foundation doesn't want to break it or make it even less usable by messing with it. So instead, after the first few D-Class splatted, they decided that everyone sent through would get a parachute. Then Nazis started splatting in the Berlin streets, so they decided to just wait until it was all over before playing with their new toy.</p>
<p>Idunno if I should edit anything now that the contest is over, but I have a feeling people might want to see more hints at what I just said here in the actual document.</p>

