<p>Pros:</p>
<ul>
<li>I like the usage of Operation Hammer. It adds a layer as to how the Foundation worked during WWII.</li>
</ul>
<p>Cons:</p>
<ul>
<li>Must we have <em>another</em> anomalous Nazi-punk device? You'd think they lost WWII due to making Wonder-weapons all the time. But on a serious note, I am honestly tired of the cliche.</li>
<li>If the Foundation already knows that it'll be raining Nazis in Berlin, why aren't they trying to empty the place right now (its population has been increasing since German reunification, and it's currently the second most populous city in the EU)? Time is of the essence here. At least if it happened in an empty Berlin, one can use the cover story of a surreal WWII film. If that happens in a populated Berlin, farewell to the masquerade. So my nitpick is the Foundation's lack of foresight.</li>
</ul>
<p>Verdict: Downvote</p>

