			<div class="content" id="post-content-2346370">
									

<p>Ok, going to address your two cons:</p>
<ul>
<li>The Nazis IRL wasted a ton of money on weapons projects that couldn't work, or that they didn't have the time to make work. Not time machines or anything like that, but a ton of other Wunderwaffe that simply wouldn't (and didn't) function. (They also built a functioning stealth fighter-bomber, which is terrifying, but they never got to use it, so it's cool.)</li>
<li>The Foundation didn't know it was going to become a Nazi thunderstorm until fairly recently. They thought it would just be a dozen or so Ahnenerbe officers, maybe a general or two (a Nazi drizzle, comparatively), not whole fucking platoons and such. It would have been a waste of effort evacuating Berlin before, and they don't have time to now. They're scrambling to come up with a cover story as it is.</li>
</ul>
<p>I knew this was risky when I wrote it. If I can rewrite it to be more entertaining after the contest, I'll look into it. Hopefully some people can get some enjoyment out of it in the meantime.</p>

